#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:149
msgid ""
"The `.` operator borrows and dereferences automatically, so you write "
"`m.translate(...)` rather than `(&mut m).translate(...)`. Method calls are "
"one of the very few places where Rust inserts a borrow for you."
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:153
msgid "Slices: the safe span"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:155
msgid ""
"A **slice** `&[T]` is a pointer plus a length, a borrowed view of contiguous"
" elements. It is `std::span<const T>`, and `&mut [T]` is `std::span<T>`, "
"except that the borrow checker guarantees the underlying storage outlives "
"the view and does not reallocate under it. `&str` is the same for UTF-8 "
"text, the safe `std::string_view`."
msgstr ""

