#: src/appendix/contributing.md:19
msgid "How translations work"
msgstr ""

#: src/appendix/contributing.md:21
msgid ""
"English Markdown under `src/` is the single source of truth. Each "
"translation is a [gettext](https://www.gnu.org/software/gettext/) catalog, "
"`po/<lang>.po`, that maps every English paragraph, heading, list item and "
"table cell to its translation. At build time the "
"[`mdbook-i18n-helpers`](https://github.com/google/mdbook-i18n-helpers) "
"preprocessor swaps the translated text in. Code blocks are shared, so "
"examples never drift between languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/appendix/contributing.md:29
msgid ""
"When an English paragraph changes, the old translation is marked _fuzzy_ and"
" the English text is shown until a translator updates it. A translation can "
"therefore lag behind without ever breaking the build or showing outdated "
"content as if it were current."
msgstr ""

#: src/appendix/contributing.md:34
msgid ""
"Interactive diagrams are written in English in `theme/js/diagrams.js`. Their"
" strings are translated in `theme/js/i18n-<lang>.js`, a plain table from the"
" English string to the translation; missing entries fall back to English."
msgstr ""

